1
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:09,770
So we moved here in 1963.

2
00:00:09,770 --> 00:00:11,320
There was nothing here on the property.

3
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:18,470
We had a camp across the creek until we had this bridge behind me built in 63, 64.

4
00:00:18,470 --> 00:00:25,350
And then after we got the bridge done, we built the little cabin that's behind Jaemyun.

5
00:00:25,350 --> 00:00:28,360
I don't know if you can see it yet.

6
00:00:31,250 --> 00:00:34,600
for that that was built in like '64.

7
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:37,710
We had no electricity, no water.

8
00:00:37,710 --> 00:00:40,330
We just had a tent on a platform.

9
00:00:40,330 --> 00:00:42,670
Took down the platform, or the tent,

10
00:00:42,670 --> 00:00:45,000
and built the little house.

11
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,420
And then we still didn't have electricity or water,

12
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:54,020
but we managed to use a headlight and a battery for lights.

13
00:00:54,020 --> 00:01:02,320
And then we just used buckets, I guess, or bottles for water until we had a spring built that was up on the hill that we built

14
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:06,060
and we had water midway through summer and then we ran out.

15
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:12,040
And then we added onto the cabin three times!

16
00:01:15,170 --> 00:01:20,040
And then in 1990, we built the big house

17
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:22,680
and that's where mom and dad lived.

18
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:28,340
And then when they passed, Gene and Patty had moved up here. to take care of the property

19
00:01:28,340 --> 00:01:33,100
and now he is my caretaker of the property

20
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:34,740
and he's doing a great job.

21
00:01:34,740 --> 00:01:39,890
And it's been a great place to have, to be raised and grow up

22
00:01:39,890 --> 00:01:41,840
and have all this to ourselves.

23
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:43,880
So it's been a blessing.

24
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:46,330
We used to have a dam under the creek

25
00:01:46,330 --> 00:01:50,390
and we would, as kids, we would all have inner tubes and air mattresses

26
00:01:50,390 --> 00:01:56,250
and we would play in the creek all afternoon till we were like blue-lipped.

27
00:01:56,250 --> 00:01:58,470
and it we finally came out

28
00:01:58,470 --> 00:02:02,080
and we could only get in the creek after we got our chores done in the morning

29
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:04,640
and then in the afternoon we could play in the creek

30
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:06,820
so it was a lot a lot of fun

31
00:02:06,820 --> 00:02:09,540
and i'm grateful that we have this property

32
00:02:09,540 --> 00:02:16,570
and Jaemyun and to do this little video and Kelly and the other little kids that are running around here

33
00:02:16,570 --> 00:02:19,850
so it's been  a treat

34
00:02:19,850 --> 00:02:25,910
can you explain the why the people called the The Dry Creek here?

35
00:02:25,910 --> 00:02:38,400
The creek itself is called Dry Creek, not because it ran dry of water, because when back in the 1800s or 1890s, whenever it was, the gold rush was going on, they never found any gold in the creek,

36
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,050
so they named it Dry Creek,

37
00:02:40,050 --> 00:02:41,720
and that's how it's got his name.

38
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:45,220
And then our creek, Dry Creek, feeds a lake downstream

39
00:02:45,220 --> 00:02:46,950
called Collins Lake,

40
00:02:46,950 --> 00:02:49,560
and it's a pretty good-sized lake.

41
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:51,210
It's known for fishing.

42
00:02:51,210 --> 00:02:53,220
they stock it like three times a year

43
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:55,270
which is good

44
00:02:55,270 --> 00:03:00,660
the cabin was built in mid 60s early 60s

45
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:02,570
and it was just the front part

46
00:03:02,570 --> 00:03:03,850
and that's where we stayed

47
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:08,360
uh my mom and dad and Gary, Gene, Sue and myself

48
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:10,860
we just stayed in that front part of the cabin

49
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:16,300
and then through the years it got added on to three times

50
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:23,500
and then in 2007, I think it was,

51
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:25,180
we had a water line break

52
00:03:25,180 --> 00:03:26,720
and it flooded the whole place.

53
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:27,540
Nobody was up here

54
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:29,600
and the water ran for three weeks.

55
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:31,740
So we had to strip it right down the inside,

56
00:03:31,740 --> 00:03:35,940
strip it all the way down to the studs so the building would dry out and wouldn't get moldy.

57
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:40,100
And then it became storage area

58
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:45,050
and then in Today our year is 2026,

59
00:03:45,050 --> 00:03:48,780
so in 2023... I started rebuilding it

60
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:50,750
and I put all new electrical in it

61
00:03:50,750 --> 00:03:53,960
and all new plumbing, siding, windows,

62
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:56,260
and just rebuild it so

63
00:03:56,260 --> 00:03:57,710
I could stay in there and live

64
00:03:57,710 --> 00:04:01,770
and be happy.

65
00:04:01,770 --> 00:04:07,560
So if he goes over here, you can see the back deck and the porch and the back part of the cabin, which is nice.

66
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:08,800
So we call that the cabin

67
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:11,470
and then the other, the house over here,

68
00:04:11,470 --> 00:04:13,030
we just call it the big house.

69
00:04:13,030 --> 00:04:15,780
And that's where we have all of our dinners and everything.

70
00:04:15,780 --> 00:04:18,590
What's the difference between the house and cabin?

71
00:04:18,590 --> 00:04:19,840
Just because this was a cabin.

72
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:21,030
We stayed in for a long time.

73
00:04:23,270 --> 00:04:26,170
Mom had to sleep upstairs, and she fell down the stairs,

74
00:04:26,170 --> 00:04:29,170
so they had to build the house to make it level

75
00:04:29,170 --> 00:04:34,380
As they were getting up in age and didn't have to worry about falls anymore.

76
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:37,610
And the cabin is small. The house is big.

77
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:38,890
Big, okay. Yeah.

78
00:04:38,890 --> 00:04:41,360
And then my mom's memorial bell.

79
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:43,100
I don't know if they got a picture of that yet,

80
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:45,130
but that's right behind them here.

81
00:04:45,130 --> 00:04:46,540
Right behind you.

82
00:04:46,540 --> 00:04:49,290
See the the thing up on the top?

83
00:04:49,290 --> 00:05:00,030
That was my mom's memorial bell that we built and this was mining equipment that we found up in the hills.

84
00:05:00,030 --> 00:05:03,200
We used to go exploring up there, some of the old mines and everything,

85
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:05,700
and this is just some of the stuff that we picked up.

86
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:10,120
The bell is actually from Depoe Bay in Oregon.

87
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:11,340
And I found that,

88
00:05:11,340 --> 00:05:14,600
so that's when I made the memorial bell for mom.

89
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:16,930
when did you make it when did you make it

90
00:05:16,930 --> 00:05:18,730
Must have been 2006.

91
00:05:18,730 --> 00:05:22,630
2006. Yeah. Almost 20 years ago. Yeah. Yeah.

92
00:05:22,630 --> 00:05:23,810
Almost or is?

93
00:05:23,810 --> 00:05:26,120
Yeah.

94
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:27,790
Anyway, that's all I got.

95
00:05:27,790 --> 00:05:31,770
You know, this is the area that we have and grew up on.

96
00:05:31,770 --> 00:05:34,610
And now Jaemyun and Kelly get to enjoy it

97
00:05:34,610 --> 00:05:37,220
and the kids too.

98
00:05:37,220 --> 00:05:37,890
Yeah. All right.

99
00:05:37,890 --> 00:05:39,750
Thank you.

100
00:05:39,750 --> 00:05:41,420
Who are you?

101
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:43,180
I'm Wayne.

102
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:46,100
Uncle Wayne, as the kids call me.

103
00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:47,590
Okay, thank you.
